  "foaf:name": "Ogyre Fishing for Litter",
  "sdo:name": "Ogyre Fishing for Litter",
  "sdo:description": "Fishing For Litter is Ogyre’s regenerative solution to combat marine plastic pollution, creating value from ocean waste, while supporting coastal communities and fostering critical ocean knowledge. Local fishermen play a central role by recovering plastic waste directly from the ocean and other coastal ecosystems. Once collected, the waste is managed by local communities, who oversee its recycling or responsible disposal, ensuring the best possible end-of-life treatment in compliance with local laws. Each step is thoroughly traceable on our blockchain-enabled platform: on one hand, fishermen can track their recollection efforts and get financial backing; on the other hand, the impact is measured real-time and publicly disclosed. Various data and relevant KPIs are gathered and analysed with the support from experts and research centres to further understand the complex interactions between marine ecosystems, pollution and local communities.",
  "sdo:location": "Italy",
  "sdo:identifier": "49.8",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/ogyre-fishing-for-litter/",
